icialArea":69.44,"website":"http://www.wolverhampton.gov.uk/"},"summary":{"extract":"Wolverhampton is a city and metropolitan borough, in the West Midlands, England. Located around 12 miles (19 km) north-west of Birmingham, it forms the north-western part of the West Midlands conurbation, with the towns of Willenhall and Walsall to the east, and the towns of Sedgley and Dudley to the south. The population in 2021 was 263,700, making it the third largest city in the county after Birmingham and Coventry.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/West_Midlands_Metro_tram_approaching_Wolverhampton_railway_station_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7798867.jpg/330px-West_Midlands_Metro_tram_approaching_Wolverhampton_railway_station_-_geograph.org.uk_-_7798867.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolverhampton"},"twins":["Q170287"],"climate":{"temp":[3.2,3.4,5.1,8,11.1,14.2,16,15.6,13.2,9.9,6.1,3.8],"rain":[65,53,53,48,61,67,72,72,52,78,73,71],"cloud":[79,78,76,73,74,76,74,76,73,77,77,80]}}